1. Visual Studio Code Setup
Step 1: Download Visual Studio Code from its official website.
Step 2: Install VS Code on your computer.
Step 3: Open VS Code.
Step 4: Create a new folder for your assignment
2. Node.js Setup
Step 1: Download Node.js from its official website.
Step 2: Install Node.js.
Step 3: Open the terminal in VS Code.
Step 4: Type the following commands:
node -v
npm -v
Step 5: Press Enter to check the installed versions.
3. Live Server Setup
Step 1: Open VS Code.
Step 2: Click on the Extensions icon.
Step 3: Search for Live Server.
Step 4: Click on Install.
Step 5: Create a file named index.html.
Step 6: Write some basic HTML code.
Step 7: Right-click on the HTML file and select Open with Live Server.
Step 8: The webpage will open in your browser.
